mod_datalynx changes
====================

2026-08-11
----------

- Fields: added the **Schedule** field type. One field holds either a single date
  and time or a weekly pattern - weekdays, a time of day and the period it runs -
  and knows which of the two it is. Because a one-off carries the weekday of its
  own date, one query serves both: searching for a date finds the ride booked that
  day *and* every commute that runs on that weekday, and a rule can match a one-off
  request against a recurring offer. Searching and matching are day-granular by
  default; a narrower tolerance is a per-field setting.
- Itinerary: stops no longer carry a planned time, and the field no longer offers
  "require a time for every stop". A route says where a journey goes, not when: a
  date on a stop could not describe a ride that runs every Monday, and a ride
  entered without one was invisible to the time check and so matched every route it
  overlapped. Use a Schedule field beside the route instead. The unread
  `timeplanned` column is dropped from the derived waypoint index.
- Rules: the itinerary "within tolerance" relation is gone with it; the same
  relation on a Schedule field replaces it, and as an ordinary search criterion
  rather than a post-filter, so it narrows before the match limit applies.
- Ridesharing: `cli/migrate_ridesharing_schedule.php` converts an existing board -
  its pattern radio button, weekday multi-select, time select and the dates on its
  routes - onto one Schedule field, and rewires the views, the matching rules and
  the search form. It reports every entry whose old fields contradicted each other
  rather than guessing silently.

2026-08-10
----------

- Rules: the **Event notification** rule can now look for other entries that match
  the one an event touched, and notify the people behind both. Each row of the new
  **Matching entries** block compares one field against the value the triggering
  entry holds for it: the same value, a different value, within a tolerance of it
  (time, number and duration fields, and an itinerary's departure), or a route that
  can carry it. New recipients "authors of matching entries" and "this entry's
  author, once per matching entry" go with it, along with an optional record of
  announced pairs so nobody is introduced twice, shareable between rules.
- Rules: the **Notify matching ride offers and requests** rule type is gone; it is
  an ordinary event notification now. Existing rules are migrated automatically
  into a pair of event-notification rules that share one record of announced pairs
  (one per side of the ride-type field), and the pairs already announced are carried
  over. The upgrade also finishes the removal - its table, message provider, version
  record and queued ad-hoc tasks - so no manual uninstall is needed and cron is not
  left suspended on a missing plugin.
- Email views: added the `##notificationotherentryurl##` and
  `##notificationotherentrylink##` patterns. When a notification is about a pair of
  entries they point at the counterpart of the one being rendered, so a message can
  show the ride that was found and still link back to the reader's own entry.
- Filters: fixed four defects in the "NOT" search path that also affected ordinary
  filters — an OR criterion matching nothing broke the query, a negated duration
  returned exactly the entries it was meant to exclude, a negated time excluded the
  entries that hold no time at all and negated a range only in part, and a negated
  multi-select dropped the entries with no value for the field.

2026-06-29
----------

- Views: added a per-view **permitted filters** whitelist. A view keeps its
  configured filter (now labelled **Default filter**) and can list additional
  filters users may switch to; any other filter is rejected and the default is
  applied. The legacy "filter override" option is now **Allow all filters** and
  supersedes the whitelist. Existing views are migrated so their behavior is
  unchanged. Backup/restore and older backups are supported.
- Rules: added the **Update field** rule type, which writes a fixed value into a
  text, select, radio button, checkbox or multi-select field when triggered
  (with optional follow-up events).
- Rules: event-notification and update-field rules support multi-row **trigger
  conditions** combined with AND/OR and optional NOT.
- Entries: added **timesubmitted** ("Time of final submission"), shown via the
  `[[timesubmitted]]` tag with the `entrytime` field format; set when an entry
  reaches Final submission and cleared if it is moved back.
- Field formats: radio button fields gained a **Stepper progress** display format
  (with optional FontAwesome step icons).
- Fields: the **Text** field type gained a responsive **Input field width**
  setting (value + px/%/em unit).
- Field layouts: the layout editor gained curated Bootstrap-5 **presets**; field
  layouts were renamed from "renderers". Fieldgroup subfields can carry their own
  layout/behavior, and a `:totals` field format adds a numeric totals row.
- Permissions: added capability `mod/datalynx:editfinalsubmission` to allow
  editing entries after they reach Final submission status.
- Documentation: updated the user guides (Views, Rules, Fields, Field Formats,
  Permissions, Patterns & Styling) to cover the above.

2026-04-20
----------

- Updated the bundled PDF.js third-party library to 5.6.205.
- Added `thirdpartylibs.xml` and `pdfjs/readme_moodle.txt` to document the
  vendored PDF.js library and its upgrade process.
